  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nUnseasonably cool through Friday then near normal \ntemperatures this weekend through early next week. Any \nsignificant storm systems stay well south of the region.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nA northerly flow will result in below normal temperatures today\nthrough Friday. A weak area of low pressure at the surface will\nslide across the region today, while a short wave rotates\naround the 500 mb low across the Canadian Maritimes. This will\nresult in unsettled weather with showers. It will be cold enough\nfor some snow to mix in across the north this morning. The 500 \nmb low meanders to our east across Canadian Maritimes tonight \nthrough Friday with continued northerly flow. Tonight is mainly\ndry. But there may be just enough diurnal instabilty in place \nfor a stray shower on Friday with the upper low still \ninfluencing the region. \n\nBy Saturday, temperatures moderate, becoming near normal as an\nupper level low exits the area Friday night and high pressure \nsettles in for the weekend. Upper level ridging builds in early\nnext week which should keep any storms systems south of the \nregion and favor seasonable temperatures.",
